# TorpedoAUV (REMUS 100 class) on ArduSub with the torpedo frame of firmware/patches/ardusub-torpedo-frame.patch,
# loaded after ArduPilot's default_params/sub.parm.
# BiguaSim model: dynamics.uuv.TorpedoAUV, 37 kg, fins +-20 deg, propeller -1525..1525 rpm.

# Torpedo frame: MOT1 propeller, MOT2 / MOT3 top / bottom rudder, MOT4 / MOT5 left / right stern plane.
# The fins only act while the vehicle moves; depth is held by pitching.
FRAME_CONFIG    8
MOT_PWM_MIN     1100
MOT_PWM_MAX     1900

# One IMU sample per physics step (200 Hz): ArduPilot wants them at 1.8 x its loop rate or more.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 100

# Depth through pitch: the stern planes give ~0.5 rad/s^2 of pitch at cruise speed, and the climb demand (the
# frame's climb factor) and the pitch loop both drive them. ArduSub's default depth gains (made for vertical
# thrusters) banged the planes between +-20 deg and swung the depth by 3 m; these hold it within 0.1 m offline,
# with a weak pitch angle hold (it would fight the climb) and pitch rate damping.
PSC_D_POS_P     0.5
PSC_D_VEL_P     2
PSC_D_ACC_P     0.1
PSC_D_ACC_I     0.02
ATC_ANG_PIT_P   0.5
ATC_RAT_PIT_P   1.0
ATC_RAT_PIT_I   0

# Heading with the rudders (as weak as the planes): after a turn the default yaw rate gains overshot 11 deg and
# drifted 8 deg back; these overshoot 3 deg and hold within 2 deg.
ATC_RAT_YAW_P   1.0
ATC_RAT_YAW_I   0.1
